# Streaming-mode nullable-fallback sample (docs/projects/
# ai_tooling_next_steps.md, ParserGenerator streaming codegen): a
# nullable, non-empty factored suffix is legal when it is trailing-
# fallback-equivalent -- every sibling after it is a strict epsilon,
# dead under ordered choice because the nullable suffix always matches
# first (pg_choice_unit_is_nullable_fallback in analysis.w). `value` is
# the shape's minimal form: after factoring the shared IDENT, the WS?
# suffix becomes the whole choice body and the dead epsilon is dropped.
# `pair` puts the nullable suffix mid-alternatives: the guarded NUMBER
# suffix still dispatches first on its first set, WS? is emitted as the
# final else branch, and the trailing epsilon alternative is dropped as
# dead. generated_streaming_fallback_test.w drives both rules over real
# input; streaming_guard_reject.pg pins the sibling shape that stays
# rejected.
parser streaming_fallback
mode streaming

token IDENT letters
token NUMBER digits
token WS = [ \t]+
literal SEMI ";"
literal COMMA ","

start document

rule value = IDENT WS? | IDENT
rule pair = IDENT NUMBER | IDENT WS? | IDENT
rule statement = SEMI value | COMMA pair
rule statement_list = statement statement_list |
rule document = statement_list EOF
